UID:legislature-senate-committee-on-natural-resources-20260921T0900@calenda
 rs.changesaroundme.com
DTSTAMP:20260827T043204Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260921T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260921T120000
SUMMARY:Texas Senate: Natural Resources
LOCATION:Room E1.012\, Texas Capitol Extension\, 1100 Congress Ave.\, Austi
 n\, TX 78701
URL:https://capitol.texas.gov/tlodocs/89R/schedules/html/C5802026092109001.
 HTM
DESCRIPTION:Summary Agenda\n\n1. Monitoring: SB 494 and SB 1806 and HB 48 f
 rom the 2025 session\n2. Study: "Ensuring Responsible Renewable Energy Dec
 ommissioning"\n\n—\n\nSB 494: relating to the establishment of a theft o
 f petroleum products task force\;SB 1806 2025 session\, relating to the in
 spection\, purchase\, sale\, possession\, storage\, transportation\, and d
 isposal of petroleum products\, oil and gas equipment\, and oil and gas wa
 ste\; creating criminal offenses and increasing the punishment for an exis
 ting criminal offense\;\n\nSB 1806: relating to the inspection\, purchase\
 , sale\, possession\, storage\, transportation\, and disposal of petroleum
  products\, oil and gas equipment\, and oil and gas waste\; creating crimi
 nal offenses and increasing the punishment for an existing criminal offens
 e\;\n\nHB 48: relating to the creation of an organized oilfield theft prev
